93e5913563b4" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265901 1145 "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate od $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ x & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ x & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\ y & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(3\\sqrt{2},3\\sqrt{2}).$" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265903 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265904 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265905 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265906 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265907 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1041 "selection" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265906 13194139533918 true] [17592186265902 1110 #uuid "774a89f7-9ae3-5415-b7d7-7ec8885d5975" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265903 1034 "(-3,-\\frac{1}{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265903 1111 #uuid "dd8a5005-c0ae-5ac5-8e59-40bd6284e726" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265904 1034 "(-3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265904 1111 #uuid "bd74836d-bdad-5231-8960-30d3bd87b611" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265905 1034 "(-\\frac{3}{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265905 1111 #uuid "ebf88997-6b46-5779-8627-ffb5f21c0dfe" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265906 1034 "(3\\sqrt{2},3\\sqrt{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265906 1111 #uuid "137986cd-bae7-5166-8185-7c24c15f3bbe" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265907 1034 "(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265907 1111 #uuid "aab39890-41b2-55fe-8e41-de736216ccc9" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265908 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265909 13194139533918 true] [17592186265908 1089 "q-86619" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265908 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533918 true] [17592186265908 1100 "The point $A$ has polar coordinates $(r,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ and the point $B$ has polar coordinates $(\\frac{r}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$  Find the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ given that the Cartesian coordinates of $A$ are $(3\\sqrt{2},3\\sqrt{2}).$" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265908 1113 #uuid "dbdb76b1-154e-56f4-8c53-1a3f3061c333" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265908 1145 "First, we use the Cartesian coordinates of $A$ to find $r,$ the distance between $A$ and the origin:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{2})^{2}+(3\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+18} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the polar coordinates of $B$ are\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=(3,\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nNow, we convert $B$ to Cartesian coordinates. To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{3}{2}).$" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265910 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265911 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265912 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265913 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265914 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1041 "selection" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265913 13194139533918 true] [17592186265909 1110 #uuid "d4df8eef-e36f-5a3e-ab1b-7f3cc68d497f" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265910 1034 "(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{3}{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265910 1111 #uuid "45540c78-9e69-5f00-95fb-ed2690378cfe" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265911 1034 "(-\\sqrt{3},3)" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265911 1111 #uuid "6ecf2784-822a-58b8-b2ba-f7e819ffd3c1" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265912 1034 "(3,3\\sqrt{3})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265912 1111 #uuid "e8a925bb-9cd0-5b16-8b7e-ad218de9f1e3" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265913 1034 "(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{3}{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265913 1111 #uuid "b50a1caa-b927-5265-a694-1bdf2b5ddaa7" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265914 1034 "(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2})" 13194139533918 true] [17592186265914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533918 true] [17592186265914 1111 #uuid "24cc3c30-cbee-5b85-bb53-cbe94ef9511f" 13194139533918 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-120311" 17592186265792 "q-12031